\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Comparison of Monte Carlo radiative transfer results using the new Rosseland mean opacity (from $\tau =1$ window algorithm) versus full frequency-group calculations. Left: 100-cell simulation with exponential density profile showing approximately 25\% deviation. Right: single-cell simulation with uniform temperature showing excellent agreement. The discrepancy in the multi-cell case arises from temperature gradients, which the gray formalism does not account for.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
